WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.048 --> 00:00:05.109
One quiet afternoon, something extraordinary happened.

2
00:00:31.408 --> 00:00:33.089
"Snort, snort, OOOOOOOOOOIIIIINNK, snort," cried the little pig.

3
00:00:33.109 --> 00:00:33.810
He seemed to be in pain.

4
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:34.670
"Why don't you look after your animals?"

5
00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:34.971
Sarah shouted.

6
00:00:34.991 --> 00:00:35.731
"What's the matter, Gub-Gub?"

7
00:00:35.751 --> 00:00:36.432
Dr. Dolittle asked.

8
00:00:36.452 --> 00:00:40.094
"He ate something bad, of course," Sarah said.

9
00:00:40.114 --> 00:00:43.857
"No, he hurt his foot," the doctor said.

10
00:00:49.241 --> 00:00:50.281
did you know that?"

11
00:00:50.902 --> 00:00:51.622
Sarah asked.

12
00:00:52.723 --> 00:00:56.305
"Well, I think Gub-Gub told me," he answered.

13
00:00:56.325 --> 00:00:58.527
"Are you out of your mind?"

14
00:00:59.047 --> 00:00:59.668
she shouted.

15
00:01:00.468 --> 00:01:04.431
"Animals can't talk!"

16
00:01:04.451 --> 00:01:09.874
"Maybe I am crazy," Dr.

17
00:01:09.914 --> 00:01:11.255
Dolittle said to himself.

18
00:01:12.376 --> 00:01:13.216
"No, you're not.

19
00:01:14.017 --> 00:01:15.698
You're talking to me right now!"

20
00:01:16.439 --> 00:01:17.820
Polynesia pointed out.

21
00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:21.342
"But you're a parrot," the doctor replied.

22
00:01:25.204 --> 00:01:28.427
"You understood Gub-Gub," Polynesia continued.

23
00:01:28.447 --> 00:01:30.228
"But that's impossible!"

24
00:01:30.896 --> 00:01:32.417
Dr. Dolittle sat up.

25
00:01:33.618 --> 00:01:37.601
"Dr. Dolittle, you have the gift," the parrot said.

26
00:01:37.621 --> 00:01:38.861
"What gift?"

27
00:01:39.282 --> 00:01:40.202
the doctor asked.

28
00:01:40.222 --> 00:01:44.605
"You can understand animal language," she answered.

29
00:01:46.967 --> 00:01:49.449
Dr. Dolittle was very excited.

30
00:01:49.469 --> 00:01:53.131
"I didn't know animals have their own language!"

31
00:01:53.611 --> 00:01:54.892
he said to Polynesia.

32
00:01:54.912 --> 00:01:56.833
"Most humans don't.

33
00:01:57.214 --> 00:02:01.476
But animals speak to each other just like people do," she said.

34
00:02:01.496 --> 00:02:06.017
"Animals also talk to people all the time.

35
00:02:06.038 --> 00:02:07.898
'I'm HUNGRY!'

36
00:02:07.918 --> 00:02:09.579
'I don't want to play!'

37
00:02:09.599 --> 00:02:11.279
'I'm HUNGRY!'

38
00:02:11.299 --> 00:02:13.700
'Oh, look at the yarn!

39
00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:15.080
Jump, Muffin!

40
00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:16.480
Jump, kitty!'

41
00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:27.504
'Meow, Meow, Meow'" "Then why can't people learn animal language?"

42
00:02:27.544 --> 00:02:28.824
Dr. Dolittle asked.

43
00:02:29.624 --> 00:02:34.525
"Only those who truly love animals can learn it," nodded Polynesia.

44
00:02:34.545 --> 00:02:38.867
"Yes, I do love animals very much," admitted the doctor.

45
00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:42.147
Every day, Dr.

46
00:02:42.187 --> 00:02:45.788
Dolittle studied the animal language with Polynesia's help.

47
00:02:45.808 --> 00:02:50.770
"Animals don't always talk with words," Polynesia whispered.

48
00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:56.311
"We can speak with our eyes, our tails, our feet with everything.

49
00:03:00.956 --> 00:03:02.577
What do you think Jip is saying?"

50
00:03:02.597 --> 00:03:06.839
"It looks like he is playing," the doctor answered.

51
00:03:07.479 --> 00:03:09.040
Polynesia shook her head.

52
00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:14.482
"But what he's really saying is: 'Get off my back, you annoying flea!'"

53
00:03:16.983 --> 00:03:19.624
It wasn't easy to learn the animal language.

54
00:03:20.424 --> 00:03:22.605
Dr. Dolittle made many mistakes.

55
00:03:22.625 --> 00:03:28.648
"This one wants to live in the garden, but the other one doesn't," the doctor observed.

56
00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:33.221
"Listen more carefully, Doctor," said Polynesia.

57
00:03:33.241 --> 00:03:37.343
"Squeak, squeak, JEEEEEEEEEEEPPPPPP!

58
00:03:38.663 --> 00:03:39.923
Jeep, Jeep, squeakkkkk!"

59
00:03:40.464 --> 00:03:41.424
cried one mouse.

60
00:03:41.444 --> 00:03:45.245
"OH!" the doctor shouted excitedly.

61
00:03:45.265 --> 00:03:48.706
"He stepped on her feet so she's angry with him!"

62
00:03:48.726 --> 00:03:50.347
"That's right!

63
00:03:50.667 --> 00:03:52.567
And he didn't even say sorry!"

64
00:03:53.168 --> 00:03:54.028
squeaked the mouse.

65
00:03:56.272 --> 00:03:57.133
Soon Dr.

66
00:03:57.173 --> 00:04:00.996
Dolittle could speak and understand the animal language perfectly.

67
00:04:01.016 --> 00:04:06.141
"Oh, please, someone help me," the horse cried.

68
00:04:06.161 --> 00:04:08.303
"I'll help you," Dr.

69
00:04:08.343 --> 00:04:09.804
Dolittle gently answered.

70
00:04:09.824 --> 00:04:13.648
"You can speak our language?"

71
00:04:14.228 --> 00:04:15.249
the horse whispered.

72
00:04:15.269 --> 00:04:19.413
"Yes. Now tell me what the problem is," said the doctor.

73
00:04:19.433 --> 00:04:26.121
"I'm so thirsty and hot, but the old man won't give me any water!"

74
00:04:26.661 --> 00:04:27.662
complained the horse.

75
00:04:28.802 --> 00:04:31.784
"You can have some water from my garden," Dr.

76
00:04:31.824 --> 00:04:32.844
Dolittle offered.

77
00:04:32.864 --> 00:04:37.286
"You seem to understand animals," the old man said.

78
00:04:37.306 --> 00:04:39.807
"You should be an animal doctor."
